From 3c84f63f1216c46c776e50812744aa19ba299bf1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: forge-shepherd <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 5 Jul 2026 23:32:30 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] fix(migrate): gate first-use Beads import with an in-DB
 marker, not a file sentinel
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Replace PR #298's file sentinel (.git/forge/beads-import.json) with a row in the
broker's kernel_migrations ledger (id data_import_beads_jsonl). A file sentinel
survives a kernel.sqlite delete, so resetting the kernel would skip re-import and
leave issues dark again — the exact footgun. An in-DB marker shares the DB lifecycle,
so a reset self-heals. The marker is success-only: a failed import records nothing and
retries (with a nudge) next command, so transient failures self-heal too.

Also hook the KERNEL_TOOL_COMMANDS branch (export-first upgraders) and thread the
kernel driver through for the ledger read/write. Verified adversarially: bulk
importIssues writes only to the read-model tables and enqueues zero projection-outbox
rows, and export targets .forge/kernel jsonl not the committed store, so there is no
data-mutation risk — no roundtrip mitigation needed. Imported issues arrive unclaimed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
